ny possible ways are there to arrange a presidency meeting under the following conditions:\n\ni. The club must choose one of the $3$ schools at which to host the meeting, and\n\nii. The host school sends $2$ representatives to the meeting, and each of the other two schools sends $1$ representative.', 'Solve the following problem step by step.\nEnd your response with a line starting with Final Answer: followed by the final result.\n\nProblem: Which is a chemical compound?\n\nA. aluminum\nB. carbonated water\nC. sodium chloride\nD. carbon-14\n\nThe final result is the letter of the correct option.', 'Solve the following problem step by step.\nEnd your response with a line starting with Final Answer: followed by the final result.\n\nProblem: Barry wants to make a huge salad using only cucumbers and tomatoes. He will use a total of 280 pieces of vegetables. If there are thrice as many tomatoes as cucumbers, how many cucumbers will be used in the salad?', 'Solve the following problem step by step.\nEnd your response with a line starting with Final Answer: followed by the final result.\n\nProblem: Currently, Antarctica is the coldest and driest place on Earth. Paleontologists have found dinosaur fossils in rock layers below the ice. Based on this evidence, which is a reasonable conclusion about the climate of Antarctica in the past?\n\nA. Antarctica has always had the same climate as at present.\nB. At some time in the past, Antarctica was a hot, dry desert.\nC. At some time in the past, Antarctica was much warmer and wetter.\nD. At some time in the past, Antarctica was colder and wetter than it is now.\n\nThe final result is the letter of the correct option.', 'Solve the following problem step by step.\nWhen the work splits into parts that do not depend on each other (separate cases or separate quantities), solve those parts in a parallel block.\n\nWithin each parallel block:\nBegin the block with <Parallel>, then list the parts inside <Goal> and </Goal>, one per <Outline> and </Outline>, numbered 1:, 2:, ...\nWrite one path per outline with the same number, enclosed in <Path> and </Path>. A path must not use results of other paths, as the paths are generated simultaneously and independently.\nAfter the last path, combine the results of the paths in <Conclusion> and </Conclusion>, close the block with </Parallel> and continue the solution.\n\nEnd your response with a line starting with Final Answer: followed by the final result.\n\nProblem: Simplify the following expression in $x$: \\[2x+8x^2+9-(4-2x-8x^2).\\] Express your answer in the form $ax^2 +bx+c$, where $a$, $b$, and $c$ are numbers.', 'Solve the following problem step by step.\nEnd your response with a line starting with Final Answer: followed by the final result.\n\nProblem: The radius of a cylinder is doubled and its height is tripled. If its original volume was 10 cubic feet, what is its volume now, in cubic feet?']
